{
  "//": [
    "Template for .claude/launch.json — copy this file to .claude/launch.json and edit",
    "the paths for your machine. The real file is gitignored (.claude/launch.json*).",
    "",
    "RULE: this file holds machine-specific PATHS and profile config only — never",
    "credentials. Secrets come from the user environment, so they live in exactly one",
    "place per machine instead of being duplicated into every worktree's launch.json:",
    "",
    "  setx ADMIN_TOKEN     \"<your local dev token>\"",
    "  setx TMDB_API_TOKEN  \"<TMDB Settings > API > Read Access Token>\"",
    "",
    "Use the Read Access Token (the long eyJ... value), not the 32-character v3 API",
    "key beside it — they are sent differently and are not interchangeable. The sidecar",
    "refuses to start if the two are swapped (ADR-094 D5).",
    "",
    "setx only affects processes started afterwards — restart your editor/agent once.",
    "The backend also reads a gitignored .env (ADR-027); the TMDB sidecar does not,",
    "so its token must come from the environment. Real env wins over .env.",
    "",
    "The film pages (/films, their enrich routes) are behind FILMS_ENABLED and 404",
    "without it — set it on any backend config you use for film QA, as `backend` and",
    "`backend-stress` do below.",
    "",
    "backend-stress serves the HOLODEX-342 stress fixture instead of a real library.",
    "Seed it first with `go run ./testdata/stressseed`; tear the whole thing down with",
    "`rm -rf ./data/stress`. It binds the same port as `backend`, so run one or the",
    "other — never both. It reads the fixture's own committed mapping AND provider",
    "registry rather than your gitignored local ones, so the ladder and the chip row",
    "are the same on every machine (HOLODEX-347 / HOLODEX-348).",
    "",
    "enrich-stub serves every fake provider that registry names — ten personas on one",
    "node process, addressed by URL path. Start it alongside backend-stress to reach",
    "the enrichment stress profile. It binds the same port as provider-tmdb, so again:",
    "one or the other.",
    "",
    "backend-stress-9300 + web-9300 are the same stress pair on ports outside a Windows",
    "excluded range: Hyper-V/WinNAT can reserve TCP 7781-7880, and then :7800 fails to",
    "bind (`netsh interface ipv4 show excludedportrange protocol=tcp` lists it). Vite on",
    ":5174 proxies /api to :9300 via HOLODEX_API_PORT (web/vite.config). It shares",
    "./data/stress with backend-stress but not its port, so nothing stops both running:",
    "start one stress backend only — two processes on one SQLite file defeat the single",
    "writer. HOLODEX-492.",
    "",
    "backend-stress-replace-9300 serves the fixture with studio as a REPLACE field",
    "(testdata/stressseed/mappings-replace-studio.yaml), the only way to exercise studio",
    "decisions — a change, a clear, the film cascade — since the canonical mapping makes studio",
    "multi. It serves a COPY: with no stress backend running, `rm -rf data/stress-replace &&",
    "cp -r data/stress data/stress-replace`, and recopy after every reseed. Never point it at",
    "./data/stress, because boot re-derives video_studios and would collapse the ladder's",
    "multi-studio videos. Pairs with web-9300. HOLODEX-497."
  ],
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "configurations": [
    {
      "name": "web",
      "runtimeExecutable": "npm",
      "runtimeArgs": ["run", "dev"],
      "cwd": "web",
      "port": 5173,
      "autoPort": false
    },
    {
      "name": "backend",
      "runtimeExecutable": "go",
      "runtimeArgs": ["run", "./cmd/holodex", "--host", "127.0.0.1"],
      "port": 7800,
      "autoPort": false,
      "env": {
        "MEDIA_PATH": "E:/YourMediaLibrary",
        "CARD_LAYOUT": "poster",
        "FILMS_ENABLED": "true",
        "METADATA_SOURCES_PATH": "G:/source/holodex/metadata-sources.local.yaml",
        "METADATA_MAPPINGS_PATH": "G:/source/holodex/metadata-mappings.local.yaml"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "backend-stress",
      "runtimeExecutable": "go",
      "runtimeArgs": ["run", "./cmd/holodex", "--host", "127.0.0.1"],
      "port": 7800,
      "autoPort": false,
      "env": {
        "DATA_PATH": "./data/stress",
        "MEDIA_PATH": "./data/stress/media",
        "FILMS_ENABLED": "true",
        "THUMBNAIL_ENABLED": "false",
        "METADATA_SOURCES_PATH": "testdata/stressseed/sources.yaml",
        "METADATA_MAPPINGS_PATH": "testdata/stressseed/mappings.yaml"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "backend-stress-9300",
      "runtimeExecutable": "go",
      "runtimeArgs": ["run", "./cmd/holodex", "--host", "127.0.0.1", "--port", "9300"],
      "port": 9300,
      "autoPort": false,
      "env": {
        "DATA_PATH": "./data/stress",
        "MEDIA_PATH": "./data/stress/media",
        "FILMS_ENABLED": "true",
        "THUMBNAIL_ENABLED": "false",
        "METADATA_SOURCES_PATH": "testdata/stressseed/sources.yaml",
        "METADATA_MAPPINGS_PATH": "testdata/stressseed/mappings.yaml"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "backend-stress-replace-9300",
      "runtimeExecutable": "go",
      "runtimeArgs": ["run", "./cmd/holodex", "--host", "127.0.0.1", "--port", "9300"],
      "port": 9300,
      "autoPort": false,
      "env": {
        "DATA_PATH": "./data/stress-replace",
        "MEDIA_PATH": "./data/stress-replace/media",
        "FILMS_ENABLED": "true",
        "THUMBNAIL_ENABLED": "false",
        "METADATA_SOURCES_PATH": "testdata/stressseed/sources.yaml",
        "METADATA_MAPPINGS_PATH": "testdata/stressseed/mappings-replace-studio.yaml"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "web-9300",
      "runtimeExecutable": "npm",
      "runtimeArgs": ["run", "dev", "--", "--port", "5174", "--strictPort"],
      "cwd": "web",
      "port": 5174,
      "autoPort": false,
      "env": { "HOLODEX_API_PORT": "9300" }
    },
    {
      "name": "enrich-stub",
      "runtimeExecutable": "node",
      "runtimeArgs": ["testdata/enrich-stub/stub.js"],
      "port": 9100,
      "autoPort": false
    },
    {
      "name": "provider-tmdb",
      "runtimeExecutable": "go",
      "runtimeArgs": ["run", "./providers/tmdb", "--host", "127.0.0.1"],
      "port": 9100
    },
    {
      "name": "docker-compose",
      "runtimeExecutable": "docker",
      "runtimeArgs": ["compose", "up", "--build"],
      "port": 7800
    }
  ]
}
